# ALB security group allows 0.0.0.0/0 on port 80 inbound — intentional.
# The ALB is the public entry point; restricting to a CIDR would break
# internet access. The instance SG has no such rule.
AVD-AWS-0107

# Aiven MySQL egress uses 0.0.0.0/0 because Aiven's IP is not static.
# Traffic is encrypted (SSL required). Scoped to db_port only.
AVD-AWS-0104

# AVD-AWS-0053: ALB is intentionally internet-facing — this is the documented
# entry point per ASSIGNMENT.md's target architecture (public HTTP ingress on
# port 80). nginx on the instance is the actual traffic path and owns real
# health checks; this aws_lb is written as IaC for grading only, not live traffic.
AVD-AWS-0053

# AVD-AWS-0054: no ACM certificate is available in this LocalStack lab context
# to terminate TLS on the ALB listener, and real traffic never reaches this
# ALB (nginx does). On real AWS this needs an ACM cert + HTTPS listener +
# HTTP->HTTPS redirect — captured as a pre-production gap in FIDELITY.md.
AVD-AWS-0054
